Z||000003||FieroJoe||05-10-2001||10:43 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by wkayl:<BR><B>I put one with temp and compas out of a 2000 Chev Silverado.  Black-ground. Pink-ign. Green-backup (I didn't hook this one up). 2 other wires went to the temp sensor installed in front of the radiator.<BR></B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>What do you mean by backup?  Backup lights?  Why would you need to have a control on there when going in reverse?<P>I have been thinking about one of those for a while now, they run about $250-300 new, what have you been paying at the junkyard for the chevy truck one?<P>------------------<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/joesig_1.jpg"> <BR>'87 Coupe 5spd.<BR>AIM:FieroJoe87||||reg||1
Z||000004||wkayl||05-11-2001||12:16 AM||||On my truck (I have a 2001 Silverado) it cancels out the nightime dimming when you put it in reverse so you can see behind you better.||||reg||1
